\section{Independent automatic-differentiation check of the $l=2$ TPV source}
\label{app:adcheck}

As an independent check on the reduced $O(\alpha_B\Omega^2)$ source, we reconstructed
the four-dimensional metric, Christoffel symbols, Riemann tensor, Ricci tensor, Weyl
tensor, normalized fluid four-velocity, and magnetic Weyl tensor directly from the
Hartle background. Coordinate derivatives were generated by automatic differentiation
rather than by using the analytic TPV source expressions.

The even-parity $l=2$ perturbation was introduced as an \emph{additive independent}
metric variation,
\begin{align}
 \delta g_{tt}&=-2N^2 h\,P_2,\\
 \delta g_{rr}&= 2A^2 b\,P_2,\\
 \delta g_{\theta\theta}&=2r^2 k\,P_2,\\
 \delta g_{\phi\phi}&=2r^2\sin^2\theta\,k\,P_2,
\end{align}
with $\delta g_{t\phi}=0$ for the independent even-parity variation. This bookkeeping
is important. The product $k\,\omega$ that appears if the compact Hartle line element
is expanded multiplicatively is of higher order in the slow-rotation hierarchy and is
not an independent $l=2$ variation.

At a representative interior point,
\begin{equation}
 r=4.968897990\ {\rm km},
\end{equation}
we chose a generic perturbation jet with nonzero
$h,h',h'',k,k',k'',b,b'$. The analytic reduced action predicts the coefficient
\begin{equation}
 C_{\rm red}
 =
 NAr^2\mathscr L_2
 =
 2.108929477739\times10^{-2}.
\end{equation}
The same coefficient was extracted independently from the full four-dimensional
quantity $\sqrt{-g}\,B_{\mu\nu}B^{\mu\nu}$ by centered finite differences in the
rotation and $l=2$ bookkeeping parameters after automatic differentiation of the
coordinate dependence. The results were
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccc}
\toprule
$\epsilon$ & $\eta$ & $C_{\rm AD}/C_{\rm red}-1$\\
\midrule
$4.0\times10^{-3}$ & $4.0\times10^{-4}$ & $1.274\times10^{-3}$\\
$2.0\times10^{-3}$ & $2.0\times10^{-4}$ & $3.185\times10^{-4}$\\
$1.0\times10^{-3}$ & $1.0\times10^{-4}$ & $7.961\times10^{-5}$\\
$5.0\times10^{-4}$ & $5.0\times10^{-5}$ & $1.990\times10^{-5}$\\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
The observed convergence orders are $2.0006$, $2.0001$, and $2.0000$, as expected for
the centered finite-difference extraction. Extrapolation is therefore consistent with
the analytic coefficient.

As a bookkeeping diagnostic, replacing the independent additive $l=2$ variation by a
multiplicatively factorized metric in which the $O(\Omega)$ frame-dragging term is also
multiplied by the $l=2$ spatial deformation produces an $O(1)$ disagreement in this
test. The automatic-differentiation calculation therefore independently confirms the
slow-rotation ordering used in deriving the TPV source.

This check is local and does not by itself replace the global Hartle--Thorne integration.
It is nevertheless independent of the finite-difference source-generation procedure
used in the stellar calculation and directly validates the reduced variational
coefficient from which the compact $l=2$ source is constructed.

